span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 68:11\" href=\"/Psalms.68.11\">ψ 68:11</a> <em>thy troop dwelt in it</em> (Thes SS RVm Hi Ri Che, but 𝔊 𝔖 Jer Pe <em>thy</em> (<em>living</em>) <em>creatures</em>, of the people; Hup <em>id.</em>, ref. to quails; improb.); <span dir=\"rtl\">אַל־תִּתֵּן לְחַיַּת נֶפֶשׁ תּוֹרֶךָ חַיַּת עֲנִיֶּיךָ אַל־תִּשְׁכַּח לָנֶ֫צַח</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 74:19\" href=\"/Psalms.74.19\">ψ 74:19</a> <em>give not the soul of thy turtle-dove to the wild beasts, the life of thine afflicted do not forget for ever:</em> RV Hi Pe Bae Sch render thus, giving <span dir=\"rtl\">חית</span> diff. meanings in the two clauses, the former being archaic fem. abs. Ges<sup>§ 80, 2. R. 2</sup>; text doubtless corrupt, read poss. <span dir=\"rtl\">למות</span> Schr Ri, for <span dir=\"rtl\">לחית</span>, or <span dir=\"rtl\">לשׁחת</span> Kroch; Gr either of these; Che either, or better <span dir=\"rtl\">לחרב</span>.", "note": true}]}, "rid": "BDB03025", "strong_numbers": ["2416"], "next_hw": "חָיֶה", "prev_hw": "חַיָּה", "all_cited": true, "ordinal": "II.", "quotes": [], "GK": ["2651", "2652", "2653"], "TWOT": ["644a", "644c", "644d"], "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "BDB Dictionary", "language": "heb.biblical", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "BDB Dictionary", "attribution": "F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs", "index_title": "BDB", "version_title": "A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906", "version_lang": "en", "should_autocomplete": true}}, {"headword": "חַי", "parent_lexicon": "BDB Aramaic Dictionary", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": "<strong>adj. living (</strong>BH id.<strong>)</strong>;—"}, {"senses": [{"definition": "of God: cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">חַי</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:31\" href=\"/Daniel.4.31\">Dn 4:31</a>, emph. <span dir=\"rtl\">חַיָּא</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:21\" href=\"/Daniel.6.21\">6:21</a>, <a data-ref=\"D